      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Recurring events are a must-have feature for our community.\n\nWe run at least six weekly events, and having to manually recreate each event every single time is exhausting and inefficient.\n\nI strongly request support for recurring events. These events need to be reliable and flexible:\n\n - It should be possible to cancel a single occurrence without deleting the entire series.\n\n - There should be an option to pause/freeze the whole series if needed.\n\n - Most importantly, the event itself must not be deleted, and subscribers to the event must not be lost.\n\n \n\nThis is critical because it allows events to build and maintain their own audience. If subscribers are preserved, we don't need to post announcements to the entire group every time just to notify people - only those who are actually interested will receive notifications.\n\nAdditionally, for security and moderation reasons, only the event creator or a main group admin should be able to delete an event. In large groups with many event organizers, compromising a single account should not allow someone to delete other organizers events and wipe out their subscriber base.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
